# Target Version Scope (Mandatory)

This project targets **EXVS2 Over Boost (OB) and earlier revisions only**.

## In scope

- **OB** — `vsac27_Release.exe`, `OBHK0.3_v27`. Primary reference image for all
  native evidence, corpus validation and address anchors.
- **XB / VS2 / MBON / FB** — historical context only. Usable for cross-generation
  comparison; never as the sole proof for a shipped field name or constant.

## Out of scope

**Any revision later than OB.** For those revisions:

- Do not target them, do not open, decompile or research their binaries.
- Do not commit native addresses, function names, field hashes, offsets, binary
  identities (path, size, SHA-256), corpus samples or field evidence from them.
- Do not use them as a validation or cross-check reference, and do not cite them
  as an evidence tier in `docs/`.
- Do not add their name, abbreviation or executable name to source, comments,
  tests, fixtures, docs or commit messages.

## Evidence rule

Every native anchor committed to this repository must be traceable to an in-scope
binary. If a finding can only be sourced from an out-of-scope revision, leave it
**unproven** and mark it as pending in-scope revalidation. Do not import the
out-of-scope anchor "temporarily".

## When you encounter an existing reference

Treat it as a defect. Re-anchor the claim to OB if possible, otherwise downgrade
it to unproven and remove the out-of-scope reference. Report it rather than
silently leaving it in place.

